  - On a base case it has been checked offline only (the self-test, `diag_c155_a1_1_facts.md:19-21`). No LabVIEW run has measured it.
  - So the planned scratch run is the first measurement of it, which is exactly what PD378(b) asks for (`ring-p5.md:157`). This is a novelty, not prior art.

**PART C — user rules**
- C1: No contradiction. The queue carries only the 1.2 → 1.7 data stream (U4, `ring-p5.md:130-131`). The rows are PD374 and PD376 unchanged, so the computation is the same (U1). The plan has no control-signal queue, no camera-loop wait and no serial call.

